SUMMARY:🍂 Fall Walk of Toronto Island 🌊🌆! 9KM
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🍂🌊 FALL WALK: TORONTO ISLA
 NDS 🌊🍁\n\n### Island Paths\, Fall Colours & Toronto's Best Urban Esc
 ape\n\nThere is something magical about the Toronto Islands in the fall.\n
 Once the summer crowds disappear\, the islands become quieter and more pea
 ceful. The changing leaves\, crisp air\, open green spaces\, quiet cottage
 s\, and golden light over the water make it one of the best times of year 
 to explore.\nAnd then there's the skyline.\n\nFrom the islands\, you get s
 ome of the best views of Toronto anywhere in the city — especially when 
 the fall colours frame the downtown skyline across the water.\n\nJoin us f
 or a relaxed fall walk through **Hanlan's Point\, Centre Island\, and Ward
 's Island**\, enjoying the scenery\, fresh air\, and great conversation al
 ong the way.\nThis is approximately **9 km**\, with mostly flat paths and 
 no major hills. It's a longer walk\, but the pace will be relaxed and we'l
 l take breaks along the way\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Gr
 oup – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n
 \n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll take the **10:15 AM Ward'
 s Island Ferry** and begin our walk once we arrive.\n\nOur route will take
  us through:\n🌿 Hanlan's Point\n🍂 Centre Island\n🏡 Ward's Island\
 n📸 Skyline viewpoints\n🌊 Waterfront pathways\n🍁 Fall foliage and 
 quiet island roads\n\nWe'll stop along the way to enjoy the scenery\, take
  photos\, have a snack\, and spend some time getting to know each other.\n
 \nAlthough we'll pass several beaches\, **we won't be stopping at them dur
 ing this event**. We have a route to follow and a ferry to catch!\n\nOur r
 eturn ferry will be the **2:45 PM Ward's Island Ferry** back to downtown T
 oronto.\n\nExpect approximately **3½ to 4 hours**\, including the ferry r
 ides and breaks.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nThe isla
 nds can feel quite different from downtown Toronto\, especially in the fal
 l. Expect cooler temperatures\, wind off the lake\, and changing weather.\
 nPlease dress in layers and bring a jacket or sweater.\nThis is a **social
  walk\, not a guided historical tour**. I'll share interesting facts along
  the way\, but the focus is enjoying the islands together.\n\n***\n\n## 
 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** **INSIDE the Jack Layton 
 Ferry Terminal after your ticket has been scanned.**\nWe are meeting **ins
 ide the paid waiting area beside the washrooms.**\n**Please do NOT wait ou
 tside the terminal.**\n\nOnce your ferry ticket has been scanned\, walk in
 to the waiting area and you'll find me wearing my **Moose Hat**. 🫎\n\n
 ⏰ **Meetup Time:** **10:00 AM**\n🚢 **Ward's Island Ferry LEAVES AT:**
  **10:15 AM**\n\nPlease be on time. **Once the ferry leaves\, it will be e
 xtremely difficult to catch up with the group.**\n🚢 **Return Ferry:** 2
 :45 PM from Ward's Island\n🎟️ **Ferry Ticket:** $9.19\n\nYou must pur
 chase your ferry ticket **before signing up for the event.**\n[CLICK HERE 
 FOR FERRY TICKETS](https://secure.toronto.ca/FerryTicketOnline/tickets2/in
 dex.jsp)\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-trans
 fer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the grou
 p and allows us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n
 \n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n
 🥨 A snack\n🧥 A warm fall jacket or sweater\n🕶️ Sunglasses\n📸
  Camera or phone for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis wal
 k is great for:\n\n* Anyone who loves fall 🍂\n* People who enjoy explor
 ing Toronto's parks\n* Anyone looking for a longer but easy walk\n* People
  who enjoy beautiful scenery and photography\n* Anyone who wants to meet n
 ew people\n* People who want to escape the city without actually leaving i
 t\n\nThe activity is the container. **The people you meet along the way ar
 e the real experience.**\n\n***\n\n**Come for the island paths.**\n**Stay 
 for the fall colours.**\n**Leave feeling like you spent the day on vacatio
 n — without ever leaving Toronto.** 🍂🌊\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP a
 head of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedu
 le.\nSometimes plans change and events may need to be cancelled\, so pleas
 e keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**
 \n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandou
 tings@hotmail.com**
