SUMMARY:🌿 FALL WALK - Walk: Tommy Thompson Park (Come See The Skyline) 
 🐦 - 12KM
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🍂🐦 Fall Walk: Tommy Thomps
 on Park 🌊\n\n### Wildlife\, Lake Views & One of Toronto's Best Fall Wal
 ks\n\nLooking for a walk that feels like you've left the city without actu
 ally leaving Toronto?\n\nJoin us for a fall walk through **Tommy Thompson 
 Park**\, one of Toronto's most unique outdoor spaces.\nThe park is famous 
 for its wildlife and birding\, with **more than 300 species recorded**\, a
 s well as its beautiful views across Lake Ontario and back toward the Toro
 nto skyline.\nIn the fall\, the cooler air and quieter trails make this a 
 particularly nice time to explore the park. We'll follow the trails toward
  the **lighthouse**\, take a break along the way\, and then make our way b
 ack.\n\nIt's a **long walk**\, but the terrain is generally easy. The goal
  is to enjoy the scenery\, get some fresh air\, and spend a few hours walk
 ing and talking with other people.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **What
 sApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKA
 nc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet near the pavi
 lion and begin our walk through Tommy Thompson Park.\n\nAlong the way we'l
 l:\n\n* Explore the park's trails 🌿\n* Look for birds and other wildlif
 e 🐦\n* Enjoy views of Lake Ontario 🌊\n* Take in the Toronto skyline 
 🌆\n* Make our way toward the lighthouse\n* Stop for a break and some ph
 otos 📸\n* Loop back to the pavilion\n\nThe walk will take approximately
  **3 hours\, including a break**.\nThis is a longer walk\, so you should b
 e comfortable walking at a steady pace for several hours.\n**No dogs are p
 ermitted in the park.**\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nT
 his is an outdoor walk\, and Tommy Thompson can be exposed to the wind com
 ing off Lake Ontario.\nPlease dress appropriately for the weather and brin
 g comfortable walking shoes.\n\nThe trail isn't particularly difficult\, b
 ut **the distance is the challenge**. If you're not comfortable being on y
 our feet and walking steadily for around three hours\, this may not be the
  right walk for you.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Loc
 ation:** Near the pavilion and bathrooms\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose H
 at!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.*
 *\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Tommy Thomp
 son Park Pavilion\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person o
 r e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support
  the group and allows us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.
 \n\n***\n\n## 🍔 After the Walk\n\nOnce we've finished\, you're welcome 
 to join us for lunch at **Wendy's or Tim Hortons** nearby.\nIt's completel
 y optional\, but it's a great chance to sit down\, refuel\, and continue t
 he conversation after the walk.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Wa
 ter\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧥 A fall jacket or s
 weater\n📸 Camera or phone for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?
 \n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy nature and wildlife 🐦
 \n* Anyone interested in birdwatching\n* People who love waterfront walks\
 n* Anyone looking for a longer social walk\n* People who want to explore s
 omewhere different in Toronto\n* Anyone who enjoys getting outside and mee
 ting new people\n\nThe activity is the container. **The people you meet al
 ong the way are the real experience.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of 
 time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSom
 etimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed\, so p
 lease keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Math
 ew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutin
 gs@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the wildlife.** 🐦\n**Stay for the conver
 sation.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 
 🍂💛
