SUMMARY:👻 Ghost Tour: The Exhibition Grounds 🎡
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n👻 Ghost Tour: The Exhibition Gr
 ounds 🎡\n\nToronto's Haunted Fairgrounds\, Dark History & One Building 
 I Don't Like Being Near\n\nThe Exhibition Grounds have spent more than a c
 entury hosting crowds\, celebrations\, soldiers\, shows\, and some of Toro
 nto's biggest events.\nBut underneath all that history is a darker side.\n
 \nThe Exhibition Grounds are said to be **one of the most haunted places i
 n Toronto** — and I'll be honest: **this is the one place on my ghost wa
 lks that genuinely scares me.**\n\nThere's something about the atmosphere 
 here.\nSome buildings have an energy that feels different. And when you kn
 ow what happened in them\, it's hard not to look at them a little differen
 tly.\n\nOn this evening ghost walk\, we'll explore the grounds and hear st
 ories of **soldiers\, settlers\, performers\, animals\, tragedies\, and pe
 ople who may never have completely left.**\n\nThis isn't just about trying
  to scare you.\nIt's about discovering the strange history hiding undernea
 th one of Toronto's most familiar landmarks.\n\n👻 What We'll Explore\nW
 e'll begin outside **Medieval Times** and make our way across the Exhibiti
 on Grounds toward the Princes' Gates.\n\nAlong the way\, we'll hear storie
 s connected to:\n\n* 🏚️ **The General Service Building**\n* 💀 **Th
 e Stanley Barracks** — the building that genuinely creeps me out\n* 🐎
  **The Horse Palace**\n* 🏠 **Scadding Cabin**\n* 👻 Other strange sto
 ries\, unexplained encounters\, and haunted corners of the grounds\n\nWe'l
 l finish at the **Princes' Gates**.\nWe'll keep a steady walking pace and 
 **will not be entering any of the buildings**.\n\n🕯️ Why This One Is 
 Different\n\nI've done a lot of ghost walks around Toronto.\n**This is the
  one that actually makes me uncomfortable.**\n\nMaybe it's the history. Ma
 ybe it's the buildings. Maybe it's simply knowing what happened here and t
 hen standing there after dark.\nWhatever it is\, the Exhibition Grounds ha
 ve always felt different to me.\n\nSo come prepared for some genuinely cre
 epy stories — and maybe a few moments where we all wonder whether we sho
 uld really be standing there. 👻\n\n🧢 Meetup Details\n📍 **Meetup L
 ocation:** In front of **Medieval Times**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose 
 Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minut
 es**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶‍♂️ **Pace:** Ste
 ady walking pace\n🏁 **End Point:** **Princes' Gates**\n\n🎟️ Meetup
  Fee\n**$10 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 \\*\\*[mathewmaclean@hotm
 ail.com**](http://mathewmaclean@hotmail.com%2A%2A/)\n\nThis is a **curated
  ghost-walking experience**\, rather than one of our regular social walks.
  The route\, stories\, and history have been researched and brought togeth
 er specifically for this experience.\nThe fee helps support the time and w
 ork that goes into creating these walks.\n\n🎒 What to Bring\n👟 Comfo
 rtable walking shoes\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n💧 Water\n📱 
 Your phone for photos\nAnd maybe… don't wander off by yourself. 👻\n\n
 🌈 Who Is This For?\nThis experience is great for:\n\n* 👻 People who 
 love ghost stories\n* 🏙️ Anyone fascinated by Toronto's darker histor
 y\n* 🕯️ Fans of the strange and unexplained\n* 🎡 People who want t
 o see the Exhibition Grounds differently\n* 🚶 Anyone looking for someth
 ing unusual to do on an evening out\n* 😈 People who like being scared 
 — at least a little\n\nYou don't have to believe in ghosts.\n**You just 
 have to be willing to walk into the dark with us.**\n\n**REMEMBER:** You'r
 e welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsur
 e about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be 
 cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates
 .\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or emai
 l:\n📧 \\*\\*[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**](http://torontomovie
 sandoutings@hotmail.com%2A%2A/)\n\n**Come for the history.**\n**Stay for t
 he ghost stories.**\n**And try not to look too closely at the buildings.**
  👻
