SUMMARY:🍂 Fall Walk: Rouge National Urban Park and Picnic🌳
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🍂🌳 Fall Walk: Rouge Nation
 al Urban Park 🌳🍁\n\n### A Real Hike\, Beautiful Fall Colours & a Pic
 nic Together\n\nWant to get out of the city without actually leaving Toron
 to?\n\n**Rouge National Urban Park** is Canada's only urban national park 
 — and one of the most popular hikes we do.\nOnce you get onto the trail\
 , it can be hard to believe you're still in Toronto. Forest paths\, rollin
 g hills\, changing leaves\, and quiet stretches of wilderness make this fe
 el much more like a trip outside the city than a walk through it.\nAnd fal
 l is one of the best times to experience it.\n\nThis is **a real hike**\, 
 though. There are some hills and ups and downs\, so it isn't the best choi
 ce if you're looking for an easy\, flat walk.\nBut if you're up for the ch
 allenge\, there's something satisfying about reaching the end knowing you 
 did it together.\nAnd then we'll have a picnic. 🧺\n\n📱 Don't forget 
 to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H5
 9mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🥾 What We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet at *
 *Don Mills Station** and take the 85C bus together toward Rouge National U
 rban Park.\nOnce we arrive\, we'll begin our hike through the park.\nAlong
  the way we'll:\n\n* Hike through forest and open spaces 🌳\n* Enjoy the
  fall colours 🍂\n* Navigate the hills and changing terrain\n* Take in s
 ome beautiful views\n* Stop for a short break along the route\n* Finish at
  the Park's Welcome Centre\n* Have a **30–40 minute group picnic** after
 ward 🧺\n\nThe hike takes approximately **2½ hours**\, plus a short bre
 ak.\nAfterward\, we'll take some time to relax\, eat\, and enjoy each othe
 r's company.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nThis is a **
 moderately challenging hike**\, not a casual stroll.\nThere are hills\, un
 even sections\, and some ups and downs\, so good walking or hiking shoes a
 re important.\nPlease come prepared for typical fall weather and bring eno
 ugh water for the hike.\n\nIf you're comfortable walking for a couple of h
 ours and handling some elevation changes\, you'll be fine.\nIf you're look
 ing for something completely flat and easy\, **this probably isn't the wal
 k for you.**\n\n***\n\n## 🚌 Meetup Details\n\n### 🚇 By TTC\n\n📍 *
 *Meetup Location:** Don Mills Station — on the platform for the **85C bu
 s**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **9:45 AM
 **\n🚌 **Bus Leaves:** **10:06 AM sharp**\nI'll wait for the bus\, but i
 f you miss it\, **you won't be able to join the group afterward.**\n**Earl
 y is on time. On time is late.**\n\n### 🚗 By Car\n\nParking is **not av
 ailable at our TTC meeting point.**\n\nIf you're driving\, please park at 
 the **Toronto Zoo** and walk to the **Park's Welcome Centre (the house)**.
 \n🚗 **Car Meetup Time:** 11:00 AM\n\nWe may be a few minutes late arriv
 ing\, depending on the bus and traffic.\n\n***\n\n## 🧺 The Picnic\n\nAf
 ter the hike\, we'll have a **30–40 minute group picnic** at the end.\nP
 lease bring something small to share — nothing too large or heavy. The g
 oal is simply to have something to eat together after the hike.\n🥪 Sand
 wiches\n🍎 Fruit\n🍪 Snacks\n🥤 Drinks\nWhatever is easy to carry an
 d share is perfect.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details at a Glance\n\n🥾 *
 *Hike:** Approximately 2½ hours + short break\n🧺 **Picnic:** 30–40 m
 inutes\n🏁 **End Point:** Park's Welcome Centre\n💲 **Meetup Fee:** $5
  cash or e-transfer\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 
 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n🥾 Good walking shoes or hiking shoes\n🥪
  A snack\n🧺 Something small to share for the picnic\n🧥 A fall jacket
  or layers\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis hike is great for:\n
 \n* People who enjoy a little challenge\n* Anyone who wants to explore Rou
 ge National Urban Park\n* People who love fall colours 🍂\n* Hikers look
 ing for a social outing\n* Anyone comfortable walking hills and uneven ter
 rain\n* People who want to meet others while getting outside\n\nThis isn't
  the easiest walk we do.\n**But sometimes the harder walks are the ones yo
 u remember.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on t
 he day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and 
 events may need to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye on the 
 event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post o
 n the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Com
 e for the hike.**\n**Stay for the picnic.**\n**Leave with a new connection
  — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛
